+### Removing a user from an organization
+
+`DELETE /orgs/{orgID}/users/{uid}` (offboarding) deletes the user's memberships
+in every project of the organization, and returns 204.
+
+- Only org admins of that organization may call it. Other organizations' paths
+  → 404. A non-admin in the same organization → 403.
+- The target user must belong to the organization; an unknown user, or one in
+  another organization → 404. A user with no memberships there → 204 (no-op).
+- Archived projects are included. Removing a membership is not a task write, so
+  the archived-project 409 rule does not apply to it.
+- Only memberships are removed. The user row, its org admin flag, and tasks
+  assigned to the user are left as they are.
+
 ## Seed data
 
